8. Violations

Permissions under this license terminate automatically upon noncompliance.
The following cure rules provide an opportunity for reinstatement, not
permission to continue prohibited activity.

Before you first receive a written notice of noncompliance under this license
from the Licensor or its authorized representative, your permissions are
automatically reinstated when you fully comply and take practical steps to
remedy past violations. Such pre-notice reinstatement does not consume the
first-notice cure opportunity below.

On your first receipt of such a notice, you have 32 days to fully comply and
take practical steps to remedy the violations. Your permissions are
automatically reinstated upon completing that cure within the period. All
noncompliance identified in the first notice, together with reasonably
related defects arising from the same incident and clarified during that
period, is handled under this single cure opportunity. Additional notices,
descriptions, or clarifications during that period do not restart or extend
the 32-day period.

After this first-notice cure, a later, independent violation does not qualify
for automatic reinstatement. If the cure period expires without full
compliance, automatic reinstatement is unavailable. These rules do not
prevent a Licensor from separately authorizing reinstatement in writing.

The notice must identify the Software and alleged noncompliance in reasonable
detail. Receipt must be supported by evidence and determined in accordance
with applicable law; sending or publicly posting a notice alone does not
establish receipt. An acknowledgment by the recipient is not the only way
to establish receipt.

Reinstatement is prospective. It does not authorize prohibited conduct during
noncompliance, waive liability or obligations for earlier violations, or
restore patent permission terminated under Section 7. Termination does not
affect rights you hold independently of this license.

